From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] winevulkan: expose VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd on Linux

Wine's Vulkan generator already knows the external semaphore FD entry points,
but hides the extension from Win32 applications.  This opt-in source patch
removes only that filter entry.  It must be applied to Wine and the generated
winevulkan sources regenerated before building the Unix/PE pair.

This is not a VKD3D fix by itself: the D3D12 interop layer still has to create
an exportable semaphore and map the fence value correctly.

---
 dlls/winevulkan/make_vulkan | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winevulkan/make_vulkan b/dlls/winevulkan/make_vulkan
index 0000000..1111111 100755
--- a/dlls/winevulkan/make_vulkan
+++ b/dlls/winevulkan/make_vulkan
@@ -133,6 +133,5 @@ UNEXPOSED_EXTENSIONS = {
     "VK_KHR_external_fence_fd",
     "VK_EXT_external_memory_metal",
-    "VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd",
     "VK_KHR_wayland_surface",
     "VK_KHR_xlib_surface",
     "VK_MVK_macos_surface",
